## Observation Logging

When a surprising result is reported, do not immediately explain it as certain. First write a neutral observation, then generate multiple competing explanations, then propose a discriminating experiment.

Prototypical surprises in this project:
- Train loss oscillates but eval ppl converges well
- A more conservative mode performs worse on forgetting than a permissive one
- Slot utilization is non-uniform across layers or steps
- Phase 2 training improves Phase 1 eval (the QA paradox)
- Freeze outperforms decouple (the decay-to-zero problem)

